# Scratch workspace .gitignore — inverse whitelist
#
# Philosophy: ignore EVERYTHING by default, then explicitly allow only the
# small set of infrastructure files that should be tracked.
#
# This prevents accidental commits of task state, secrets, logs, credentials,
# or any other ad-hoc content that lives in a scratch workspace.
#
# To force-track a specific file that would otherwise be ignored:
#   git add -f path/to/your-file.md

# ── Step 1: Ignore everything ──────────────────────────────────────────────
*

# ── Step 2: Un-ignore tracked infrastructure files ─────────────────────────
!.gitignore
!README.md
!AGENTS.md
!LICENSE

# ⚠️  TEMPLATE-IN-REPO EXCEPTION — READ BEFORE DEPLOYING ⚠️
# The two lines below exist ONLY because this template lives nested inside
# a larger repo (slop). They let git track this example directory.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REMOVE THESE TWO LINES when you copy this file to your own standalone
# scratch workspace. Keeping them in a standalone repo is harmless, but
# they are unnecessary and may cause confusion.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
!examples/
!examples/**

# ── HARD DENY — never track, even with `git add -f` ───────────────────────
# These patterns are anchored here so that `git add -f` on a matching path
# will be silently rejected.  If you intentionally need to track one of these
# files, rename it first to something outside these patterns.

# Secrets and credentials
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/secrets.*
**/credentials.*
**/token
**/token.*

# Cookie / browser session artifacts
**/cookie
**/cookie.*
**/cookies
**/cookies.*
**/cookiejar
**/cookiejar.*
**/*cookies.json
**/*session.json
**/*sessions.json

# SSH private keys
**/id_rsa
**/id_ed25519
**/id_dsa
**/id_ecdsa
**/*.ppk

# Kubernetes config (may contain cluster credentials)
**/.kube/
**/kubeconfig
**/kubeconfig.*

# Other common credential / secret patterns
**/*secret*
**/*password*
**/*passwd*
**/*apikey*
**/*api_key*

# TLS / PKI artefacts
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*.cer
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.der

# Cloud provider CLI state
**/.aws/
**/.azure/
**/.gcloud/
**/azure-cli/
**/gcloud/

# Logs
**/*.log
**/logs/
**/*.log.*

# Local issue tracking (dcat / dogcat)
**/.dogcats/

# Task state folders (the whole tasks/ tree is ignored)
tasks/

# Session-resume files contain task context that may include internal URLs,
# issue keys, org names, and other potentially sensitive coordination state.
# They are hard-denied here to prevent accidental force-adds.
# If you genuinely need to publish a session-resume file, sanitise it first
# and rename it (e.g. tasks/<ID>/sanitised-handoff.md) before force-adding.
SESSION-RESUME-*.md
**/SESSION-RESUME-*.md

# Editor and OS artefacts
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Python / Node / other tool caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
node_modules/
.npm/
.cache/

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
